From 75bcc0927b83ada2f003bde4bf385e8d47107807 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 03:13:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add a home-screen steps widget (ring + distance + calories
 burned)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Inspired by a reference widget screenshot the user shared. New
StepsWidgetProvider (AppWidgetProvider) draws a progress ring as a Bitmap
(RemoteViews has no native arc view) plus distance/calories stat pills,
matching the app's own steps-detail styling. Read-only, same pattern as
the existing CalorieWaterWidgetProvider:

- MiqyasWidgetPlugin.update() now also caches steps/goal/distance/
  calories/last-synced-at into SharedPreferences and force-redraws both
  widgets, not just the calorie/water one.
- docs/js/core.js's syncWidget() sends the extra steps fields whenever
  Health Connect is granted and today's steps have been cached at least
  once (computed via the already-existing estimateStepsDistanceKm/
  estimateStepsCalories helpers) -- omitted otherwise, so the widget's
  own stale-data handling shows an honest 'not synced yet' state.
- The refresh button only re-renders the last data already synced by the
  app (per the user's choice) -- no live Health Connect read from the
  widget process.

Touches android/, so this needs a new CI build (not a docs-only push)
before it reaches the installed app, and the user will need to manually
add the new 'مِقياس — الخطوات' widget to their home screen afterward.
